#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:1
msgid "Proper caching in vtkHDFReader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:3
msgid ""
"vtkHDFReader cache was reworked to work properly with all supported types "
"but vtkHyperTreeGrid, with added support for "
"vtkPartitionedDataSetCollection, vtkMultiBlockDataSet and vtkOverlappingAMR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:6
msgid ""
"The caches now ensure the MeshMTime of vtkDataSet provided by the "
"vtkHDFReader do not change if they should not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:9
msgid ""
"In this context, the UseCache member is now true by default and it have been "
"deprecated for further removal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:12
msgid ""
"GetAttributeOriginalIdName, SetAttributeOriginalIdName and AddFieldArrays "
"have also been deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:14
msgid ""
"vtkHDFUtilities::RetrieveHDFInformation have been deprecated in favor of a "
"version with more arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:16
msgid "Proper distributed support in vtkHDFReader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:18
msgid ""
"vtkHDFReader now generates proper vtkPartitionedDataSet distributed contents "
"with empty (nullptr) partitions where other ranks have data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:21
msgid "Piece distribution configuration in vtkHDFReader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:23
msgid ""
"When reading partitioned data in parallel, you can now use `vtkHDFReader::"
"SetPieceDistribution` to choose the piece distribution strategy: interleave "
"blocks between processes, or allocate \"blocks\" of partitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:26
msgid "Better support for partitioned data writing in vtkHDFWriter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:28
msgid ""
"`vtkHDFWriter` is now able to write partitioned data in parallel when the "
"number of non-null partitions differ between processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:31
msgid ""
"Removal of unspecified Temporal FieldData behavior with vtkOverlappingAMR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:33
msgid ""
"vtkOverlappingAMR does not specify properly how to handle temporal field "
"data in the VTKHDF specifications, the implementation have been removed "
"before a proper reimplementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:37
msgid "Quiet support in vtkHDFUtilities::Open"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:39
msgid ""
"A new argument have been added to vtkHDFUtilities::Open to suppress all "
"console output on error. The previous version has been deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:42
msgid "vtkHyperTreeGrid support in vtkHDFWriter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:44
msgid ""
"`vtkHDFWriter` now properly supports the HyperTreeGrid data model. It can "
"write partitioned, temporal and distributed data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:46
msgid ""
"New data types specified: vtkRectilinearGrid, vtkStructuredGrid and vtkTable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:48
msgid ""
"The VTKHDF specification now supports Recilinear Grids, Structured Grids and "
"Tables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:50
msgid ""
"`vtkHDFWriter` and `vtkHDFReader` are both capable of handling these new "
"datatypes, for simple and time-dependent data (no partition or extent "
"support)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:52
msgid "vtkHDFUtilities and vtkHDFReader deprecations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:54
msgid ""
"The protect method `vtkHDFReader::DataArraySelection` now returns a `std::"
"map` instead of a `std::array` with `vtkDataObject::AttributeTypes::` as a "
"key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkhdf-improvements.md:55
msgid ""
"`vtkHDFUtilities::GetArrayNames`, `RetrieveHDFInformation` and "
"`NewFieldArray` also use a `std::map<int, hid_t>` for the "
"`attributeDataGroup` argument instead of a `std::array<hid_t, 3>`."
msgstr ""
